From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: Fix stale soffice.data.js.link causing missing VFS directories

The Emscripten file packager generates soffice.data.js with FS_createPath
entries for all directories needed by files in soffice.data. This file is
copied to soffice.data.js.link via gb_Helper_copy_if_different_and_touch,
which only updates the target if content differs. The .link file is then
used by the linker to embed VFS setup into soffice.js.

When build flags change (e.g., adding --enable-cairo-canvas), the file
packager regenerates soffice.data.js with new directory entries, but
gb_Helper_copy_if_different_and_touch may not detect the change if the
.link file has a newer timestamp (due to .PRECIOUS preventing deletion).
This causes soffice.js to embed stale FS_createPath entries that don't
match the actual files in soffice.data, resulting in "ErrnoError: No such
file or directory" at runtime.

Fix: Remove .PRECIOUS so make can delete stale intermediates, and replace
gb_Helper_copy_if_different_and_touch with unconditional cp to ensure
the .link file always matches the latest .data.js.

diff --git a/static/CustomTarget_emscripten_fs_image.mk b/static/CustomTarget_emscripten_fs_image.mk
--- a/static/CustomTarget_emscripten_fs_image.mk
+++ b/static/CustomTarget_emscripten_fs_image.mk
@@ -1797,9 +1797,8 @@

 $(emscripten_fs_image_WORKDIR)/soffice.data $(emscripten_fs_image_WORKDIR)/soffice.data.js : $(emscripten_fs_image_WORKDIR)/soffice.data.js.metadata

-.PRECIOUS: $(emscripten_fs_image_WORKDIR)/soffice.data.js.link
 $(emscripten_fs_image_WORKDIR)/soffice.data.js.link: $(emscripten_fs_image_WORKDIR)/soffice.data.js
-	$(call gb_Helper_copy_if_different_and_touch,$^,$@)
+	cp $^ $@

 .PHONY: $(emscripten_fs_image_WORKDIR)/soffice.data.concat_lists
 $(emscripten_fs_image_WORKDIR)/soffice.data.concat_lists: $(gb_emscripten_fs_image_filelists) $(gb_emscripten_fs_image_autoinstall)
